course: dictionary
lesson: 8854
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shoemaker is a person whose job is making or mending shoes and boots. The ending -maker is a clue: a baker makes bread and a shoemaker makes shoes. «The shoemaker's shop was full of leather, tools and half-made boots» tells you the same thing. Shop, leather and tools all point to shoes.
explain: The same word can mean something different in a story. In «The Elves and the Shoemaker», a shoemaker is a character in a fairy tale. The words around it show which meaning is used: leather and tools mean the job, but elves and magic mean the character.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «My shoemaker mended my boots» makes sense if shoemaker means a person who mends shoes. Cobbler is another word for a person who repairs shoes, so you can use it as a clue too.
fact: A shoemaker is a person whose job is making or repairing shoes and boots.
fact: The ending -maker means someone who makes something: a baker makes bread, a shoemaker makes shoes.
fact: Before factories, shoemakers worked by hand with leather.
fact: «The Elves and the Shoemaker» is a fairy tale by the Brothers Grimm, in which elves secretly make shoes at night.
fact: A comet can be named after people, so a capital letter shows it is a name: «Shoemaker-Levy 9» is a comet named after the astronomers who found it, not a job.
exercise: «The shoemaker's shop was full of leather, tools and half-made boots.» What is a shoemaker here? | A person who sells vegetables at the market | A tall tree in the forest | *A person who makes or repairs shoes and boots | A bird that sings at night
exercise: In the fairy tale «The Elves and the Shoemaker», the shoemaker is a character. What does shoemaker mean in that story? | A pet dog | A shop that sells cakes | *A character in a fairy tale who makes shoes | A tall tree
exercise: Which word means about the same as shoemaker when the job is mending shoes? | Baker | Hatter | Tailor | *Cobbler
test: «In 1994 pieces of the comet Shoemaker-Levy 9 crashed into Jupiter.» Why does Shoemaker start with a capital letter here? | It is a mistake | It is an important job title | It means shoe-making | *It is part of a name
test: «The shoemaker worked by candlelight, cutting leather for the boots.» Which meaning fits best? | A kind of boat | A shop that sells socks | A person who paints houses | *A person who makes or repairs shoes
exam: Mia reads about elves and a shoemaker in a fairy tale, then reads that a comet is called Shoemaker-Levy 9. Why does shoemaker mean different things? | Shoemaker is always a comet | Shoemaker is only a fairy tale word | Shoemaker always means the same thing, so Mia is wrong | *The words around it show which meaning is used
